{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-gemini/src/paths.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:59:09.376407Z","id":"b0a413e42fe215abbe9eefd236ece78abe31d589c60e252ca9060b4186ea1528","body":{"detail":"Seen 2026-10-15 running gemini 0.47.0 in a temp HOME: new sessions are chats/session-<ts>-<id>.jsonl; a projected .json is converted on resume. paths.rs:244,294,346 filter on .json. Reading 0.47 needs the jsonl shape (header, message, $set patches), not just the extension. Individual-tier serving is gone, so this matters for enterprise accounts and archives. review/resume-matrix-v4-gemini.md","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":244},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"f9e35607630bf8aa34786d605b8ef092cf374c6e0671900ca55205df19dd602a"},"summary":"gemini-cli 0.47 writes session-*.jsonl (header + message + $set records); the adapter lists .json only, so native 0.47 sessions are invisible to derive and resolve","tags":["review","gemini","defect-candidate","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
